### Transaction Notes/Description Testing

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7071/api

### Create a transaction with detailed notes and batch information
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "fromLocationId": null,
  "toLocationId": 1,
  "quantity": 200,
  "unit": 1,
  "transactionType": 1,
  "expiryDate": "2026-01-15T00:00:00",
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2025-JAN-001",
  "notes": "Initial inventory received from supplier ABC. Quality inspection passed. Temperature controlled transport. Store in cool, dry place. Lot reference: ABC-2025-001.",
  "unitCost": 12.75
}

### Create a transfer with detailed transfer notes
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "fromLocationId": 1,
  "toLocationId": 2,
  "quantity": 50,
  "unit": 1,
  "transactionType": 3,
  "expiryDate": "2026-01-15T00:00:00",
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2025-JAN-001",
  "notes": "Transfer from warehouse to retail store. Requested by store manager John Doe. Transfer approved by warehouse supervisor. Use FIFO method.",
  "unitCost": null
}

### Create a sale transaction with customer and order details
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "fromLocationId": 2,
  "toLocationId": null,
  "quantity": 10,
  "unit": 1,
  "transactionType": 2,
  "expiryDate": null,
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2025-JAN-001",
  "notes": "Sold to customer Jane Smith. Order #ORD-2025-12345. Payment method: Credit Card. Delivery address: 123 Main St, City. Customer phone: +1234567890.",
  "unitCost": null
}

### Create an adjustment transaction with reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "fromLocationId": 1,
  "toLocationId": null,
  "quantity": 5,
  "unit": 1,
  "transactionType": 4,
  "expiryDate": null,
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2025-JAN-001",
  "notes": "Inventory adjustment due to damaged goods. 5 units found damaged during routine inspection. Reason: Package torn during handling. Disposed according to company policy.",
  "unitCost": null
}

### Update a transaction with additional notes
PUT {{baseUrl}}/transactions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "fromLocationId": 1,
  "toLocationId": 2,
  "quantity": 75,
  "unit": 1,
  "transactionType": 3,
  "expiryDate": "2025-11-30T00:00:00",
  "batchNumber": "BATCH-2025-JAN-001-UPDATED",
  "notes": "Updated transaction. Original transfer was 50 units, now adjusted to 75 units based on revised demand forecast. Updated by: System Administrator. Reason: Increased store demand.",
  "unitCost": 13.25
}

### Get transaction to verify notes are saved and returned properly
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/1

### Get all transactions to see notes in list view
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions
